      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "If ${a}_{n+2}={a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n}$ with ${a}_{1}=1$ and ${a}_{2}=6,$ then ${a}_{4}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}={a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1+2} & ={a}_{1+1}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =6+1 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=2$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2+2} & ={a}_{2+1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & ={a}_{3}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & =7+6 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${a}_{4}=13.$",
